    "paragraph": "Researchers developed the CARE-Drive framework to evaluate whether vision-language models in automated driving make decisions based on human-relevant reasons rather than post-hoc rationalizations. A separate study in Poland mapped county-level human development from 2010 to 2023 by combining the traditional scalar Local Human Development Index with a complex-number vector approach and typogram visualisations. Finally, a computational framework converted macroscopic static urban data into microscopic dynamic travel simulations for roughly 475,000 synthetic residents in Niterói, Brazil.",
